ch check, or copy-paste guard invocation the operator would actually run"],"finding":"AC3's guard does not specify its invocation/interception path, so it may not actually block the RCA'd command (a manual host-side `git fetch` run by an operator as uid 1000), reducing it to a proxy ('a guard exists') rather than blocking the dangerous fetch at the moment it runs.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f575f369c3db45e71","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, bullet 3 ('Add any lightweight script/guard that can reject or warn on a mirror recovery refspec that writes directly to protected branch refs')","norm_id":"nd94ae1912c2ccc0e","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator during a live incident copies a `+refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*` refspec and runs the raw git fetch; a repo-side guard never executes and main is moved backward again"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a proving test/fixture that feeds the known-bad refspec `+refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*` (and a safe quarantine refspec) to the guard and asserts reject/warn vs allow.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6","T2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Add any lightweight script/guard that can reject or warn on a mirror recovery refspec that writes directly to protected branch refs.'","Context names the exact offending refspec: '+refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*'","No proving command/RED fixture is described to confirm the guard actually catches this refspec."],"finding":"AC3 requires a guard that 'can reject or warn' on a dangerous refspec but describes no test/fixture that exercises the guard against the exact known-bad refspec from the RCA, so the guard's effectiveness is not provable in-session.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f62b06cc8505426e4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, line 3 ('Add any lightweight script/guard...')","norm_id":"n24871ead80b04938","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The guard is written with a regex that misses '+refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*' and silently passes the dangerous fetch through."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'Guard has a test asserting it rejects/warns on `+refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*` and any `:refs/heads/*` destination, and permits a quarantine-namespace refspec.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","resp